    "presentation": {
      "chief_complaint": "Fever and fatigue",
      "hpi": "The patient is admitted with fever and fatigue, not with a finished explanation. Temperature is 38.20 C. Dental examination shows caries and periodontal disease. There is no prosthetic valve. Two blood-culture sets drawn before antibiotics grow Streptococcus sanguinis, reported susceptible to penicillin. Ceftriaxone 2 g intravenously once daily is started after the cultures are drawn. Repeat cultures show no growth. Transesophageal echocardiography shows a mitral vegetation, mild regurgitation, no abscess, and preserved ventricular function. Cardiac surgery finds no current indication for an operation. Ceftriaxone 2 g intravenously once daily continues for four weeks from the first negative culture. Metformin and atorvastatin are continued. Discharge creatinine is 0.9 mg/dL and glucose has fallen.",
